  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "through-runtime",
      "claim": "OpenAI-compatible (openai_compatible, openai and litellm types other than Codex and Zen) and Bedrock Chat, Responses and both streams go through the llmgw-core Runtime with core's OpenAI-compatible and Bedrock verticals, registered in the per-type table. Core performs adaptation, the reasoning rename, the Responses-400 parameter retry and the Pollinations chat path; the router still converts Responses to Chat for Chat-only models; a native Responses 404 or 405 maps to the Chat fallback. The gateway's OpenAIProvider transport, OpenAIAuth, bearerAuth and bedrock.go are removed; the OpenAI-wire catalog moved into its own type and stays on the gateway path.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/openai_compatible_vertical.go, openai.go, catalog code"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "goldens",
      "claim": "New characterization goldens for Bedrock and OpenAI-compatible edges (forced adaptation, keyless Pollinations, a 429 refusal) were recorded with the previous code and pass unchanged with the new code; no existing golden changed.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/testdata/characterization/bedrock.golden, openai-compatible-edges.golden"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "credentials",
      "claim": "API keys resolve in the factory's order (personal connection, system connection, configured key); no key, free or none sends no Authorization for keyless servers and the anonymous kilo, llm7, OVH and Pollinations modes; public is sent as the bearer; a Bearer prefix is stripped.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers OpenAI-compatible tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "deviations",
      "claim": "Edge-case differences: soft-error messages no longer quote upstream text; a Retry-After date is passed as seconds; Bedrock refuses non-region names and non-absolute base URLs and inference times out after 300 seconds by default (documented in docs/PROVIDERS.md); Chat served over Responses drops extra fields with a warning instead of refusing; Responses for a model missing from the catalog is labelled translated, which is how it is served; numbers such as 64.0 are re-rendered as 64; keys resolve per request.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers tests; docs/PROVIDERS.md"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "claim": "The full Go suite passes with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY unreachable with unchanged existing characterization goldens; the providers config.Get budget moves from 21 to 20; gofmt, vet, govulncheck (0 reachable), check-docs and git diff --check pass.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local gate run on the reviewed head"
      }
    }
  ],
